        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-29 21:41:41.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-29 21:41:41.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_65k",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_65k\n\ntest_65k deactivates each OSC on the MDS in turn and checks\nthat manual striping still works. On DNE the loop also visited\nthe OSCs of every other MDT on that node, though only MDT0000's\ncreate counts are changed and the directory could land on any\nMDT. Each iteration also ran about 24 remote commands, and\nwaited for the OSC import on every MDT.\n\nCreate the directory on MDT0000, loop over MDT0000's OSCs only,\nwait for the import on the single MDS only, look up the OST\nindices once, and fold the per iteration lctl calls into one\nremote command each for deactivate and for restore.\n\nOn a VM with 4 MDTs (two per MDS) and 2 OSTs the test takes\n43s, 44s and 42s before and 13s, 13s and 13s after. At 17446\nCI runs per 30 days that saves about 30s x 17446 = 145 hours\nper 30 days, more on configurations with more OSTs.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=65k\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I4bf2b995b5775ba309e9b1d397f00f516e511cee\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
